Subject: [PATCH] fix(web): keep the booth idle video steady

The idle video flashed. It mounted as a black overlay about a third of a
second before its first frame played, and a mouse move or a brush of the
screen as it appeared closed it again at once, so the screen went from
the app to black and back. Movement during the hold to dismiss closed it
too, before the hold finished.

The video now fades in over the app when its first frame plays. Taps,
mouse moves and key presses neither end it nor count as activity, so the
idle reset keeps counting while it plays. Only a press or a key held for
1.5 seconds ends it. The hint says "Hold any key to try Hone yourself",
since the booth laptop may have no touch screen. While the visitor holds,
the hint reads "Keep holding" and a small ring at its left fills, so
nothing covers the middle of the video. The video takes focus, so
held keys never type into the chat below. A video that never starts
closes after ten seconds, so a stalled load cannot hide the app.

The idle time before the video now defaults to 30 seconds instead of 90.
